# Prelude No. 11 in F major, Well-Tempered Clavier I, BWV 856
# (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: a light two-part invention in a lilting 12/8. Sixteenth
# figures chase each other between the hands, and against them one hand
# holds a long trilled note for half a bar while the other keeps moving.
# Cheerful and quick, but it should sing, with a dancing four beats to
# the bar.
#
# Time signature and bars: 12/8, 18 bars, no upbeat; the MIDI has the
# same 18 bars.
#
# Tempo: dotted quarter = 72 (sixteenths about 7 a second), 72 beats,
# about 1:02. Track times (MusicBrainz track lists): Angela Hewitt
# (Hyperion, 1998) 1:02, about 70; Rosalyn Tureck 1:06 and 1:08 (two
# sets), about 65; Glenn Gould 0:57, Friedrich Gulda 0:56 and Sviatoslav
# Richter 0:55, about 76 to 79; Edwin Fischer 0:48, about 90. 72 is
# close to Hewitt, at the unhurried end of the pianists, which suits
# the chip's plucked sound and keeps the trills clear.
#
# Structure (from the Mutopia score, checked bar by bar against the
# MIDI; the keys are my reading):
#   1-2    F major: the figure in the right hand over the bass in
#          eighths, answered.
#   3-4    long trilled notes pass between the hands, half a bar
#          each (B, E, C-sharp, F), against the figure in the other
#          hand: a sequence toward D minor.
#   5-8    D minor, the figure passed between the hands.
#   9-10   the trilled sequence again, higher (G-sharp, C-sharp,
#          F-sharp, B): toward A minor and G minor.
#   11-13  through C minor and G minor; held notes in the right hand
#          over running sixteenths in the bass (13), on the dominant.
#   14-16  a long trilled B-flat in the bass (14-15) under the right
#          hand climbing to its top C: the climax.
#   17-18  the cadence in F major.
#
# Voicing: two parts throughout, so there is no middle voice to
# balance. The trills are written as plain held notes in the MIDI.
# Range: the low bass notes (D2, G2, A2, C2, F2) are lifted an octave.

tempo 72 4.          # dotted quarter, four beats to the 12/8 bar

voice mid 0          # two parts

dyn 1 mf             # bars 1-8: F major out to D minor
dyn 9 mp             # bars 9-13: the sequence through the minor keys,
                     # a softer manual
dyn 14 f             # bars 14-16: the B-flat pedal and the climb to the
                     # top C
dyn 17 mf            # bars 17-18: the cadence

rit 1 0.7            # the last bar into the final F
